From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:40:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996: Add DDR bandwidth to the GPU OPPs

The GPU's gfx-mem path is in the device tree and the OPP core finds it by
itself, but the OPPs have no bandwidth to vote for. So the GPU asks for
nothing and DDR runs at what the display asks, 6400 MB/s (800 MHz) of a
possible 1804 MHz.

Add the nominal level downstream gives each GPU frequency (qcom,bus-freq).
Downstream also moves up and down from that level at runtime, from the
GPU's memory wait counters. This does not, so it can hold DDR higher than
downstream would.

The lowest OPP stays without a vote, where downstream has 1600 MB/s:
disable_clk() parks a suspended GPU on it, and a vote there would stay on
with the GPU off. While the display is on, its own vote is higher anyway.

Tested on the Galaxy Tab S3 (SM-T820), with glmark2-es2-wayland off-screen
at 1080p, two boots each way, three rounds each:

  scene              fps before  fps after
  desktop, blur          87         111
  refract                35          45
  terrain                24          30
  texture               275         329
  effect2d              150         162

Battery current over those scenes, on USB, went from 632 to 744 mA, and
peak GPU temperature from 59 to 66 C. Terrain held 29 to 31 fps for 10
minutes, with the GPU levelling off at 76 C, against a trip at 90 C. The
vote is back at 0 when idle.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi    | 6 ++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro.dtsi | 1 +
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
index c34eae44eb..ca4f8ece65 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
@@ -1305,26 +1305,32 @@ gpu_opp_table: opp-table {
 				 */
 				opp-624000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <624000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <14432000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0x09>;
 				};
 				opp-560000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <560000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <12440000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0x0d>;
 				};
 				opp-510000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <510000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8136000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 				opp-401800000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <401800000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <6144000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 				opp-315000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <315000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <4376000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 				opp-214000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <214000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <2400000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 				opp-133000000 {
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro.dtsi
index b74cff06f3..6c5aec7099 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro.dtsi
@@ -324,6 +324,7 @@ &gpu_opp_table {
 
 	opp-652800000 {
 		opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <652800000>;
+		opp-peak-kBps = <14432000>;
 		opp-supported-hw = <0x01>;
 	};
 	opp-624000000 {
